config EXTERNAL_FREETZ_PACKAGE_FREETZ_MATTER
	depends on EXTERNAL_ENABLED && FREETZ_PACKAGE_FREETZ_MATTER
	bool "freetz-matter"
	default n
	help
		Externalizes the following file(s):
			/usr/bin/freetz-matter

		The Matter device binary is the whole payload (4.5 MB stripped), so it
		can be kept on USB/NAS storage and leave the firmware image untouched.
		The init script, the Freetz configuration and the fabric store are not
		externalized: they are tiny, needed at boot, and the store must live in
		/mod/etc anyway to survive reboots. The rs-matter stack is linked in
		statically, so the binary has no companion files to carry along.
